The function of BoHs in D&D and Nethack are actually quite fundamentally
different.

D&D bags do NOT hold an infinite amount of items. What they *do* do is that
nothing you place inside will increase the weight of the bag. A 60 pound
bag of holding will still weigh 60 pounds if it is completely empty, or if
you put a full grown elephant inside. They have fixed interior dimensions,
so infinite storage is not possible. D&D bags do not explode when you put
rods of cancellation or bags of tricks inside, but they can be ruined by
sharp objects (sheathed swords ok, bare swords bad).


